   "model": {
    "lang": "minizinc",
    "text": "% Beer distribution in MiniZinc, solved by COIN-BC (a MIP solver).\n% solver: cbc\n% Depots is a set of names, so it is an enum; the names may hold spaces.\nenum Depots;\nset of int: Bars;\narray[Depots, Bars] of int: costs;\narray[Depots] of int: supply;\narray[Bars] of int: demand;\n\narray[Depots, Bars] of var 0..10000: flow;          % an output item\nvar int: TotalCost :: output =                      % an output item\n  sum(d in Depots, b in Bars)(costs[d, b] * flow[d, b]);\n\nconstraint forall(d in Depots)(sum(b in Bars)(flow[d, b]) <= supply[d]);\nconstraint forall(b in Bars)(sum(d in Depots)(flow[d, b]) >= demand[b]);\nsolve minimize TotalCost;\n",
    "backend": "minizinc"
